  "findings": [
    "No blocker found in accepted-only release: storage for duplicate/rejected copies is freed without incrementing advertised cumulative header/data limits.",
    "Staging, per-class committed slots and six-byte DLLP buffer are separate. DLLPs bypass a TLP waiting for downstream readiness; offered/accepted whole-frame ownership is retained once selected.",
    "Integrated completer-only mode statically disables requester admission/outstanding requests; unexpected completion packets request recovery. Finite completion storage tests are component-only, not endpoint compliance.",
    "FC snapshots, CRC state and sent counters advance on handshake and accepted EOP; InitFC1/2 transitions require full local triplets and corresponding peer facts.",
    "Output arbiter locks on the first offered valid byte including stalls and inter-byte bubbles; frame ownership releases only on accepted EOP."
  ],
  "scope": "Read-only review of three new RTL modules and exact saved evidence, no native rerun or exhaustive formal proof. The 32-byte/default project frame and ready/valid backpressure boundary, cycle-count timers, no PHY/MPS interoperability and no SDF limitations remain as authored.",
